Rainbows are my favourite. I love the way they arc across the sky after a storm. They are bright and cheerful.

My favourite rainbow is the one that appears over the sea. It looks like a giant, colourful bridge. The red and orange are warm, like a sunset. The blue and purple are cool, like the deep water below.

I like rainbows because they bring hope. They show that even after a dark day, light can return. They are a reminder that things can be beautiful again.

When I see a rainbow, I feel happy. It makes me smile. It is a small, magical thing that makes the world feel better. I hope to see many more rainbows in my life. They are a gift from nature, and I am grateful for them. [end of text]


